  "usageRule": "MLB-SP1 is a starter or bulk-primary pitcher addendum, not a relief replacement. While design-scaffold or shadow, M2 may use its source/status plan and future deltas for diagnostics only. Once materialized and backtested, SP1 deltas should feed ML, F5 ML, totals, team totals, YRFI/NRFI, pitcher expected lines, batter production, HR lanes, and public game-story explanations. Rotowire primary/bulk pitcher is the projection pitcher; an MLB-listed opener is first-inning context unless the source role proves a true starter. BvP older than three seasons is context-only. HRForce >= 1.5 must tax fragile pitchers and lift supported batter/game run expectations; HRForce >= 1.7 should block casual unders unless starter, lineup, bullpen, park, and market context all explicitly support suppression."
